<figure class="viz" id="viz-stages">
  <p class="chart-title">Four jobs, and a growing bet</p>
  <p class="stage-axis">Higher on the ladder, the machine can touch more of the world. The bar lengths are a sketch of that climb.</p>
  <ol
    class="stage-ladder"
    aria-label="Four jobs. Doing sits at the top with the widest exposure bar. Looking things up sits at the bottom with the narrowest. The bars are a conceptual sketch of reward and of the room for harm. Each row includes an everyday example and where a person still sits."
  >
    <li class="stage-top">
      <div class="stage-copy">
        <p class="stage-kicker">4 · Do it</p>
        <p class="stage-name">The action lands</p>
        <p class="stage-human">A car steers itself, or an agent deletes the row, and when a wrong move would be costly a person still makes the last movement.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stage-meter" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="stage-meter-label">Widest exposure</span>
        <span class="stage-track"><span class="stage-fill" style="--fill: 100%"></span></span>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="stage-copy">
        <p class="stage-kicker">3 · Pick</p>
        <p class="stage-name">Someone chooses</p>
        <p class="stage-human">A GPS names a route, or an agent proposes the next command, and the person still chooses.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stage-meter" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="stage-meter-label">Wide exposure</span>
        <span class="stage-track"><span class="stage-fill" style="--fill: 74%"></span></span>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="stage-copy">
        <p class="stage-kicker">2 · Put it together</p>
        <p class="stage-name">A picture forms</p>
        <p class="stage-human">A summary joins several feeds, or a display forecasts where two planes will meet, and the raw feed stays available.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stage-meter" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="stage-meter-label">Moderate exposure</span>
        <span class="stage-track"><span class="stage-fill" style="--fill: 48%"></span></span>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="stage-copy">
        <p class="stage-kicker">1 · Look things up</p>
        <p class="stage-name">The world comes in</p>
        <p class="stage-human">A spell-checker reads the sentence, or a radar sweeps the sky, and the person can still see the original.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stage-meter" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="stage-meter-label">Narrow exposure</span>
        <span class="stage-track"><span class="stage-fill" style="--fill: 24%"></span></span>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption>
    A conceptual sketch. The four jobs follow{' '}
    <a href="https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/844354/">Parasuraman, Sheridan, and Wickens, 2000</a>.
    The bars illustrate the argument of this essay: reward and the room for harm grow together as the machine climbs.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
